course: dictionary
lesson: 6494
title: Almost, but not quite
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Nearly means almost, but not completely. If you are nearly ready, you are close, but you are not ready yet. The clue is in the word itself: near means close.
explain: Nearly can also tell about something that almost happened but did not. «I nearly fell» means you came close to falling, but you stayed on your feet. Try swapping in almost: if the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
explain: In maths, nearly is used with estimates. «Nearly 100» means a little less than 100, so 97 fits, but 100 exactly does not.
explain: Some useful phrases: «nearly always» means almost every time. «Not nearly» means not at all, or far from. «It is not nearly finished» means it is still a long way from finished.
fact: Nearly is an adverb, a word that tells us more about another word, here how close something is.
fact: «Nearly» means almost, but not completely.
fact: «Nearly» can also mean something almost happened but did not, as in «I nearly fell».
fact: «Much of a muchness» is an old saying that means nearly the same.
fact: Some tales are nearly true: the owl that turns its head «all the way round» really turns about three-quarters of the way, and that is amazing enough.
exercise: «A girl in Dublin ran for the bus, and one morning she nearly stepped in front of a van.» What does nearly tell us? | She missed the bus | *She almost stepped in front of the van, but did not | She did step in front of the van | She never ran for the bus
exercise: «Asia holds nearly six in ten of the world's people.» Does nearly mean exactly six in ten? | No, it means more than ten in ten | Yes, it means exactly sixty | *No, it means close to six in ten, but not exactly | Yes, it means exactly six in ten
exercise: Find the number that fits «The crowd was nearly 100.» | *97 | 150 | 120 | 100 exactly
test: «We are nearly home.» What does nearly mean here? | *Almost home, but not quite there yet | Far away from home | Lost on the way | Home already
test: «It is not nearly finished.» What does not nearly mean? | *Not at all finished, far from it | Almost finished | Finished a long time ago | Finished exactly on time
exam: Maya says «I nearly fell.» If you swap nearly for almost, what does the sentence mean? | I flew through the air | I fell and got up at once | *I almost fell, but did not | I fell over very hard
